On failed rollouts, we roll back the environment state to s t ∗ s_{t^{\ast}} and resample a single suffix under four controlled conditions:
(1) no-hint : resamples purely from the rolled-back state s t ∗ s_{t^{\ast}} without skill hints;
(2) no-hint ( t ∗ + 1 t^{\ast}{+}1 ) : rolls back state to s t ∗ + 1 s_{t^{\ast}{+}1} to evaluate temporal localization sensitivity;
(3) 3B-self : appends failure mode m ∗ m^{\ast} and self-generated skill hints from π base \pi_{\mathrm{base}} (mirroring OPSD);
(4) 8B-teacher : appends skill hints generated by a larger teacher model ( Qwen3-VL-8B , mirroring OPD).

